shared/research/recolor_preview/

# Claude — the session's own scratch stays local, but the ENFORCEMENT
# must travel: `settings.json` carries the PostToolUse/Stop hooks that
# run desktop/tests/run_guards.py (rules/CODE.md -> Enforcement), and the
# verify skill is this project's build/launch recipe. `.claude/` stays at
# the TRUE repo root (THE THREE-FOLDER MIGRATION, 2026-08-12) — it did not
# move into desktop/. `settings.local.json` is personal (per-machine
# permission grants) and stays out.
# `.claude/` is ignored EXCEPT the files a fresh clone needs to enforce the
# laws: `settings.json` carries the two run_guards hooks, `skills/` is the
# launch/verify recipe, `uv_windows.py` is the window registry `uv shot`
# imports. The blanket `.claude/` line that used to sit below this block is
# gone: git never re-includes a file under an ignored DIRECTORY, so it
# silently cancelled every `!` line here.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/uv_windows.py
.claude/settings.local.json

# Machine-written working files of the session runner (root rules/tools/uv.py)
# and the session ledger — never tracked. Listed explicitly so they stay
# ignored even if the whitelist above ever widens.
.claude/sessions/
.claude/evidence/
